Most experienced nethackers are already aware of the dramatic benefits a 
robe gives to spell casting failure rates.  However, there is a second, 
more obscure effect: even when spellcasting is otherwise hopeless, a robe 
will provide most classes with a small chance of success.  This is useful 
because, given enough mana (turns), a persistent player will eventually 
succeed in casting a crucial spell such as Remove Curse, Identify, or 
Polymorph.

The following table is based on information in spl1-343.txt.  It gives 
Maximum Fail Rates by class for characters with a robe, no shield, and no 
metal armor items.  "Emergency" spells are healing, cure blindness, cure 
sickness, extra healing, restore ability, and remove curse.  Each class 
also has a single special spell which it is especially good at; subtract 
4% for that spell only.  The special spells are listed in spl1-343.txt. 
An asterisk indicates that the special spell is also an emergency spell.

 
CLASS   NORMAL MAX FAIL RATE     EMERGENCY 
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
 Arc           95%                  95%
 Bar            -                    -
 Cav            -                    -
 Hea           93%                  90% *
 Kni           99%                  97%
 Mon           88%                  86% *
 Pri           93%                  91% *
 Ran           99%                   -
 Rog           99%                  99%
 Sam          102%                   -
 Tou           95%                  96%
 Val            -                   99%
 Wiz           91%                  91%

XL, spell level, casting skill, and INT/WIS aren't on the table, because 
no matter how bad they are, the robe still caps failure rate.  Some 
classes have caps above 99%, and so will be hopeless even with the robe, 
even when attempting their special spell.  I've indicated those with 
dashes.  


